{"causes": ["The inherent instability of the late Eastern Han dynasty fostered an environment of constant warfare and shifting allegiances among warlords.", "The ambition and strategic maneuvers of major warlords like Lü Bu and Cao Cao created a volatile political landscape for their subordinates.", "The Siege of Xiapi in 198 CE represented a critical military confrontation that forced loyalty and survival choices upon all participants."], "effects": ["Cao Xing's death contributed to the eventual downfall and execution of the warlord Lü Bu at the Siege of Xiapi in 198 CE.", "His fate serves as a minor but illustrative example of the perils of shifting loyalties and internal strife within warlord factions during the late Han dynasty.", "The elimination of Lü Bu's faction, to which Cao Xing belonged, allowed Cao Cao to further consolidate power in northern China, paving the way for the Three Kingdoms period."], "relationships": [{"sourceSlug": "lu-bu", "sourceName": "Lü Bu", "verb": "COLLABORATES_WITH", "targetSlug": "cao-xing", "targetName": "Cao Xing", "context": "Cao Xing served as a military officer under the warlord Lü Bu during the late Eastern Han dynasty."}, {"sourceSlug": "siege-of-xiapi", "sourceName": "Siege of Xiapi", "verb": "OCCURS_DURING", "targetSlug": "cao-xing", "targetName": "Cao Xing", "context": "Cao Xing's most significant historical appearance and ultimate demise occurred during the Siege of Xiapi in 198 CE."}, {"sourceSlug": "cao-xing", "sourceName": "Cao Xing", "verb": "PARTICIPATES_IN", "targetSlug": "fall-of-the-eastern-han-dynasty", "targetName": "Fall of the Eastern Han Dynasty", "context": "Cao Xing's military career and death were integral to the chaotic conflicts that marked the decline and fall of the Eastern Han dynasty."}, {"sourceSlug": "xiapi-china", "sourceName": "Xiapi, China", "verb": "OCCURS_IN", "targetSlug": "cao-xing", "targetName": "Cao Xing", "context": "Cao Xing met his end during the pivotal Siege of Xiapi in 198 CE, a strategically important city in ancient China."}, {"sourceSlug": "cao-cao", "sourceName": "Cao Cao", "verb": "CAUSES", "targetSlug": "cao-xing", "targetName": "Cao Xing", "context": "Cao Cao's military campaign against Lü Bu at Xiapi directly led to the circumstances of Cao Xing's death in 198 CE."}], "places": [{"name": "Xiapi, China", "role": "Site of death"}, {"name": "Xuzhou, China", "role": "Region of activity"}, {"name": "Han Dynasty China", "role": "Geopolitical context"}], "texts": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Cao Xing", "type": "Reference article", "slug": "cao-xing"}], "externalLinks": ["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q702993", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cao_Xing"], "tags": ["Military Leaders & Commanders", "conflict-and-resolution", "geopolitical-linkage", "temporal-linkage"], "thumbnailUrl": "", "quote": "", "legacySummary": "", "historicalSignificance": {"significanceScore": 4, "significanceNarrative": "Cao Xing's actions and death, though minor, are historically notable for contributing to the internal strife and eventual defeat of Lü Bu's faction, which was a key step in Cao Cao's rise to power.", "significanceCategory": "local"}, "_editLog": [{"timestamp": "2026-11-22T23:12:39Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#45081590684", "field": "summary", "oldValue": "Cao Xing (b. 200 CE) was a public servant or civil administrator of the Classical era, an age of empires, philosophical inquiry, and foundational civilizations, active in Global. Known in the fields of military leaders & commanders.", "newValue": "Cao Xing was a military officer serving under the formidable warlord Lü Bu during the tumultuous final years of the Eastern Han dynasty, a period marked by widespread civil strife and the fragmentation of imperial authority in what is now China. Active around 198 CE, his brief but dramatic involvement in the power struggles of the era, particularly his role in the events leading to Lü Bu's downfall, illuminates the precarious nature of loyalty and the brutal realities of warlordism that characterized the transition from imperial unity to the Three Kingdoms period.

His most notable historical appearance occurred during the pivotal Siege of Xiapi in 198 CE, where Lü Bu, besieged by the combined forces of Cao Cao and Liu Bei, made his last stand. Cao Xing was involved in an attempted mutiny by Hao Meng, another of Lü Bu's generals, who sought to betray Lü Bu to Cao Cao. Accounts suggest Cao Xing initially sided with Hao Meng but was convinced by Gao Shun, Lü Bu's loyal general, to return to his master's side. Later, during the siege itself, some historical narratives (notably from the *Romance of the Three Kingdoms*) depict Cao Xing engaging in a fatal confrontation with Lü Bu, attempting to defect or challenge him, resulting in his death at Lü Bu's hand.

While not a figure of major command, Cao Xing's actions, particularly his shifting loyalties or ultimate demise at the hands of his lord, underscore the intense internal pressures and distrust that plagued Lü Bu's camp. His death, whether a consequence of his own treachery or a desperate act of defiance, contributed to the narrative of internal decay and weakening morale within Lü Bu's forces, directly preceding Lü Bu's capture and execution. This sequence of events was a critical step in Cao Cao's consolidation of power in the north, laying foundational groundwork for the Wei kingdom."}, {"timestamp": "2026-11-22T23:12:39Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#45081590684", "field": "detailsJson.causes", "oldValue": [{"title": "Classical era: flourishing of philosophical inquiry, imperial expansion, and codification of la", "type": "EventWindow", "year": "200 CE"}, {"title": "Military conflicts and strategic necessities", "type": "Idea", "year": "200 CE"}], "newValue": ["The inherent instability of the late Eastern Han dynasty fostered an environment of constant warfare and shifting allegiances among warlords.", "The ambition and strategic maneuvers of major warlords like Lü Bu and Cao Cao created a volatile political landscape for their subordinates.", "The Siege of Xiapi in 198 CE represented a critical military confrontation that forced loyalty and survival choices upon all participants."]}, {"timestamp": "2026-11-22T23:12:39Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#45081590684", "field": "detailsJson.effects", "oldValue": [{"title": "Determined military outcomes shaping geopolitical boundaries", "type": "Idea", "year": "198 CE"}, {"title": "Contributed to enduring intellectual and institutional frameworks shaping subsequent civilizati", "type": "Movement", "year": "198 CE"}], "newValue": ["Cao Xing's death contributed to the eventual downfall and execution of the warlord Lü Bu at the Siege of Xiapi in 198 CE.", "His fate serves as a minor but illustrative example of the perils of shifting loyalties and internal strife within warlord factions during the late Han dynasty.", "The elimination of Lü Bu's faction, to which Cao Xing belonged, allowed Cao Cao to further consolidate power in northern China, paving the way for the Three Kingdoms period."]}, {"timestamp": "2026-11-22T23:12:39Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#45081590684", "field": "detailsJson.relationships", "oldValue": [{"sourceSlug": "cao-xing", "sourceName": "Cao Xing", "verb": "COMMANDS", "targetSlug": "field-280", "targetName": "Military Leaders & Commanders", "context": "Cao Xing: Military command in military leaders & commanders"}, {"sourceSlug": "cao-xing", "sourceName": "Cao Xing", "verb": "OCCURS_DURING", "targetSlug": "classical", "targetName": "Classical Era", "context": "Cao Xing was active during the Classical era"}], "newValue": [{"sourceSlug": "lu-bu", "sourceName": "Lü Bu", "verb": "COLLABORATES_WITH", "targetSlug": "cao-xing", "targetName": "Cao Xing", "context": "Cao Xing served as a military officer under the warlord Lü Bu during the late Eastern Han dynasty."}, {"sourceSlug": "siege-of-xiapi", "sourceName": "Siege of Xiapi", "verb": "OCCURS_DURING", "targetSlug": "cao-xing", "targetName": "Cao Xing", "context": "Cao Xing's most significant historical appearance and ultimate demise occurred during the Siege of Xiapi in 198 CE."}, {"sourceSlug": "cao-xing", "sourceName": "Cao Xing", "verb": "PARTICIPATES_IN", "targetSlug": "fall-of-the-eastern-han-dynasty", "targetName": "Fall of the Eastern Han Dynasty", "context": "Cao Xing's military career and death were integral to the chaotic conflicts that marked the decline and fall of the Eastern Han dynasty."}, {"sourceSlug": "xiapi-china", "sourceName": "Xiapi, China", "verb": "OCCURS_IN", "targetSlug": "cao-xing", "targetName": "Cao Xing", "context": "Cao Xing met his end during the pivotal Siege of Xiapi in 198 CE, a strategically important city in ancient China."}, {"sourceSlug": "cao-c